  {
    "sha": "d50f14a5435b939e17bd2f15e3127b0c0cc64b59",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGQ1MGYxNGE1NDM1YjkzOWUxN2JkMmYxNWUzMTI3YjBjMGNjNjRiNTk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T22:16:22Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T22:16:22Z"
      },
      "message": "refactor(pathkernel): say what the order does with a whole full-width curve and the first row\n\nReview notes of PR #4234. A curve with a Span::Whole full-width mark is\ntaken after the other ready curves and starts as a plain curve (no\nstretch end); the starts match names each case. A row on the first step\n(no tool position) is never reversed, on purpose: it runs as the\ncanonical guide set gives it. The walk builds the planned cuts once and\nremoves each cut that it takes, in place of a new list at each step.\n\nRefs #4177\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
